{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dialectal-acidotic-coati","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCut the next fix release, 0.13.1, from reviewed main using docs/releasing.md. Prior\npackage/tag: 0.13.0/v0.13.0 (currently live on PyPI and the latest GitHub Release). Only\n6 commits landed on main since v0.13.0, all internal/non-user-facing (config/plan_review\nsplit, SSM secret handling, MCP registry description-length fix, LLM cache/enrichment\ntweaks) -- CHANGELOG.md's [Unreleased] section on origin/main is empty, so step 1a is a\nno-op retitle/placeholder rather than a curated entry. PyPI is immutable; publication uses\nthe dispatch-from-main workflow and its pypi environment approval. Note: the prior release\nticket (hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo, 0.13.0) closed FAILED on the MCP Registry publish\nstep due to a navapbc org OAuth-App access restriction blocking the manual fallback after a\nsame-run PyPI-already-exists conflict; the registry currently still reports 0.13.0 as\nNOT live (0.12.0 is isLatest). This release attempt should go through the normal\nrelease.yml single-dispatch path (mcp_registry needs: publish in the same run), which is\nunaffected by that specific failure mode as long as this dispatch succeeds end-to-end in\none run; the org OAuth-App restriction only matters if the manual fallback path becomes\nnecessary.\n\n## Plan\n- Fresh worktree from origin/main (../release-0.13.1); confirm prerequisites, identity,\n  Gerrit rights, channel state.\n- Bump pyproject.toml + every server.json version to 0.13.1; regenerate uv.lock; add a\n  0.13.1 CHANGELOG section (today's date -- curate from error: VERSION is required, e.g. make changelog VERSION=v0.8.0 output if any\n  conventional commits are picked up, otherwise a minimal maintenance-release entry -- with\n  a fresh empty Unreleased section above it and updated compare links.\n- Regenerate tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json (__version__ bump) per the 0.13.0 release\n  ticket's documented new step.\n- Preflight: version-lockstep guard, release-specific tests, lint, typecheck, full test\n  suite, build, twine check.\n- Commit with DCO + Change-Id + rebar-ticket trailer; Gerrit review to LLM-Review +1 and\n  Verified +1 with no unresolved comments; Submit.\n- Dispatch release.yml from main with version=0.13.1; approve the pypi environment\n  deployment; monitor to a terminal result (including the mcp_registry job, given the prior\n  release's unresolved failure there).\n- Verify PyPI + PEP 740 provenance, GitHub tag/release + artifacts, MCP Registry (confirm\n  0.13.1 isLatest), Homebrew tap bump (trigger autobump).\n- Channel-install nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 and run the packaged post-publication probe.\n- Record receipts on this ticket; close only after all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml -- package version bump\n- server.json -- MCP manifest/package version bump\n- uv.lock -- root package version lockstep with pyproject.toml\n- CHANGELOG.md -- new 0.13.1 release section and compare links\n- tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json -- __version__ bump\n\n## Rollback / failure policy\nBefore publish: stop on any failed guard/review/CI vote; remediate via a new Gerrit\npatchset. After publish PyPI cannot be replaced: yank 0.13.1, de-list its GitHub Release,\ncut a fixed patch version; never overwrite artifacts or retag published content.\n\n## Testing\n- \n- ruff check src tests scripts\n- \n-  on the published wheel\n- rebar probe — mode: ISOLATED (temp tracker) — rebar: /Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar\n\n=== create — types, fields, and validation ===\n\n=== show — alias, short id, missing, fields ===\n\n=== edit — each field + validation ===\n\n=== tags — add, idempotent, untag (missing graceful) ===\n\n=== links — relations, cycle, self, invalid, unlink ===\n\n=== claim + optimistic-concurrency (exit 10) ===\n\n=== transition — blocked, auto-detect, backward, task close, reopen ===\n\n=== close guards — bug --class vocabulary, story/epic verdict-hash ===\n\n=== quality gates ===\n\n=== file-impact / verify-commands (+ invalid JSON) ===\n\n=== scratch set/get/clear ===\n\n=== reads — search, ready, next-batch, summary, exists, epics, descendants ===\n\n=== --output / -o — canonical structured-output flag (json|llm|text); legacy removed ===\n\n=== report --output json — summary/check-ac/quality-check/fsck/bridge fsck ===\n\n=== lifecycle --output json — create/claim/transition/reopen/delete result shapes ===\n\n=== single-reducer parity — show == list == search shape (bug f026) ===\n\n=== --help — usage without execution; free-text not intercepted ===\n\n=== archive + fsck + compact ===\n\n=== delete — friction (requires --user-approved) ===\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nPROBE RESULT: 142 passed, 0 failed (mode: ISOLATED (temp tracker)) against the channel-installed 0.13.1 build\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml declares version 0.13.1.\n- [ ] server.json top-level version is 0.13.1.\n- [ ] Every server.json packages[].version is 0.13.1.\n- [ ] uv.lock records the root nava-rebar package at version 0.13.1 and  exits 0.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md contains a 0.13.1 section dated with today's release date.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md has a fresh Unreleased section and correct 0.13.1 compare links.\n- [ ] tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json reflects __version__ 0.13.1.\n- [ ]  exits 0.\n- [ ] Release-specific guard and workflow tests exit 0 ().\n- [ ] ruff check src tests scripts exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] mypy src/rebar scripts exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ]  produces the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ]  exits 0 for the built artifacts.\n- [ ] The release commit contains DCO sign-off, a Gerrit Change-Id, and this rebar-ticket trailer.\n- [ ] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit records Verified +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit has no unresolved comments on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit submits the release change and the resulting commit is on main.\n- [ ] release.yml is dispatched from main with version input 0.13.1.\n- [ ] The required pypi environment deployment is approved.\n- [ ] Every required release.yml job completes successfully, including mcp_registry.\n- [ ] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.13.1.\n- [ ]  on the published 0.13.1 wheel with --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar exits 0.\n- [ ] GitHub tag v0.13.1 resolves to the released main commit.\n- [ ] GitHub Release v0.13.1 is marked Latest and attaches the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar version 0.13.1 as isLatest.\n- [ ] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.13.1 PyPI sdist URL with matching SHA-256 (or scheduled autobump confirmed).\n- [ ] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with zero failures.\n- [ ] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this ticket.\nEOF\n)","id":"334d-71ba-589f-4eea","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Release rebar 0.13.1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788047040346318001,"uuid":"da3fe3ad-c39f-4773-b4b5-2c99abb69d6a"}